<!--Post: 9119--><!--Time: 1109397337-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9119"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 9:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I send my prayers for them.  They are in a world of hurt at the moment.  I also send my condolences to the rest of the family ... Paula&#39;s parents Hugo and Eileen may have been taken during today&#39;s events ... and Paula&#39;s sisters Donna and Sharon are also in hurt as well ...  <BR> <BR>Please.  So that we can let them know that we care about them.  Leave a little message here.  May God look over them ...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9119-->
<!--Post: 9150--><!--Time: 1109402803-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9150"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 11:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Amen to that! They are ever bit as much vicitms as anyone else in this holocaust. Please keep all of the Rader family in your deepest prayers.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9150-->
<!--Post: 9200--><!--Time: 1109426613-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9200"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 6:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thank you for creating this thread. Their faith in God has to be the only strength they have right now. Their whole world has been turned upside down and inside out. The man they knew evidently gave little hint as to his very darkest side and secrets. I know that their church family will help uphold them, though they are in disbelief as well. <BR> <BR>This is a time when they can claim that the sea rages, the ship is battered and the sails are torn, but the Anchor holds. Only the families of the victims can truly know what the Rader family is going through and will be going through until their deaths. The Rader&#39;s faith will be an witness to others. God help us all in this fallen world. <BR> <BR>Oddly, I would venture to say that Dennis is somehow relieved that he can lay this burden down. When the full impact of what he has done to his family has been realized, he will be a truly broken man &#40;if he can muster a conscience&#41;. If he ever needed a humble and contrite spirit, it is now. Serial killers rarely commit suicide while practicing their craft. I doubt that he makes bail, so they need to place him under a suicide watch. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9200-->
<!--Post: 9280--><!--Time: 1109460511-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9280"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 3:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Will be praying for them also.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9280-->
<!--Post: 9295--><!--Time: 1109464381-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9295"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 4:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I hope the people in their town are supporting them, and remembering that they have nothing to do with this, I will pray for them also.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9295-->
<!--Post: 9318--><!--Time: 1109471956-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9318"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bestbud<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bestbud<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 6:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Did I read somewhere that the son is stationed overseas?  If so, how very sad...He&#39;s fighting for his Country and the killer in his Country is his own father...Imagine his reaction when the Red Cross notified him...My prayers continue... <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9318-->
<!--Post: 9379--><!--Time: 1109486949-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9379"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Screamer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Screamer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 10:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok, my prayers are with the family, but were there NO red flags AT ALL? Even yellow flags? I guess only they know now for sure. No disrespect towards them at all.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9379-->
<!--Post: 9394--><!--Time: 1109490240-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9394"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 11:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->there was another u.s. serial killer of fairly recent vintage who killed for years without his wife and kids knowing.  not only that, but he was a &#42;homosexual&#42; serial killer, trolling gay bars for young men.  after he&#39;d played out his bondage fantasy on them, he buried them in the backyard. <BR> <BR>his name is not coming to me... iirc he lived and hunted in the north eastern u.s..  eventually his wife started putting together the clues and brought the cops in to take a look at the bones the kids kept finding scattered around the yard. <BR> <BR>anyway, it &#42;is&#42; possible for a &#34;family man&#34; to pull this kind of double life off... and it&#39;s still totally unfathomable.  if any one can recall the guy i&#39;m referring to, he might be useful to study in terms of understanding our friendly neighborhood demon-posessed serial killer, dennis rader.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9394-->
<!--Post: 9666--><!--Time: 1109584206-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9666"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 1:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You&#39;re thinking of Herb Baumeister from Indiana.  In the meantime, keep Rader&#39;s family in your thoughts and prayers, but let&#39;s otherwise keep discussion about them to a minimum for the time being.  This is about Dennis Rader, not his family.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9666-->
<!--Post: 10053--><!--Time: 1109736672-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10053"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 8:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I read that Brian is under a suicide watch. Hopefully, he will not be his father&#39;s last victim.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10053-->
